/-!
# The original plus-A₆ moved module

The original Sylow and characteristic-two hypotheses make W_K elementary
and its faithful plus actor two-reduced. The normal A₆ component has trivial
centralizer and lies in the subgroup generated by best offenders. Its order
360 supplies the odd-prime rank bounds for the complete B.5.1 application.
The resulting moved section is Irr+ and its central quotient is the natural
four-dimensional A₆ module. The central attachment is retained explicitly.

These are the actual W_K action and component images used by the C.1.24
selection argument, without a separate module-classification assumption.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith B.5.1 and C.1.24, applied in 13.6.22, p.932.
-/

public section
open Subgroup Representation Representation.BinaryOffender Theory.GroupTheory Stellmacher
open scoped IsMulCommutative
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section06.CentralizerReduction.ComponentElimination.SourceSmallModels.OriginalAssembly.SixModels
